WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.105
The federal requirement, from NIST special
publication eight hundred fifty-three,

2
00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:08.475
revision five, as the guide's
requirements table maps it.

3
00:00:08.475 --> 00:00:12.756
Step 7 supports S C seven,
boundary protection, and A C four,

4
00:00:12.756 --> 00:00:17.037
information flow enforcement;
its evidence is the zones,

5
00:00:17.037 --> 00:00:21.500
the endpoints, and the public-access
state of each resource.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.547
Step 8 supports S C twelve, cryptographic
key establishment and management,

7
00:00:26.547 --> 00:00:30.632
S C twenty-eight, protection of
information at rest, and I A five,

8
00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:34.718
authenticator management; its
evidence is the vault posture,

9
00:00:34.718 --> 00:00:37.762
the rotation policies,
and the audit event log.

10
00:00:37.762 --> 00:00:40.498
Each row lines up with the fed-ramp twenty

11
00:00:40.498 --> 00:00:43.313
X key security indicators the guide names.

12
00:00:43.313 --> 00:00:48.254
The steps support these controls; the
organization still sets their parameters,

13
00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:51.480
and the assessor decides
whether each is satisfied.
